I've written and committed the session plan as 8b5279fa: two task files plus issue responses. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the plain git add staged nothing. I used git add -f, which is how earlier sessions got their plans in.

Task 1 (product, #742): make `/retry` use the tool name it already has. Today /retry guesses which tool failed by scanning the error text, even though the prompt loop already records the real name and the auto-retry path uses it. Before planning I read the two earlier failed attempts' receipts (#773, #779). Neither agent got as far as a diff. My reading of why, from a grep rather than a test: the tool name is dropped when control goes back to the REPL, because the REPL only stores last_error.
• **The fix:** add a sibling field that travels everywhere last_error does, in repl.rs and dispatch.rs.
• **A small pure helper** prefers the recorded name and falls back to the old text scan. It gets a table test, including a check that any path with no recorded name behaves exactly as before.
• **Commit comes before any cargo run**, and I left prompt.rs and dispatch_sub.rs alone because the earlier attempt hit size-limit trouble there.
• **Not in the risk subsystem.** That follows the trajectory's warning that risk took 2 of the last 4 self-driven changes.

Task 2 (evolve, #944 via receipt #959): per-run spend report for `scripts/daily_diary.sh`. I've re-planned it unchanged. The last attempt never actually ran the task: its log ends in a model list, which means it was running on the broken .yoyo.toml that #962 fixed earlier today. A grep confirms daily_diary.sh still has no audit logging (0 hits). The pattern to copy from scripts/social.sh is still there. The only thing I added is an explicit "commit before verifying" step.

